; Engine configuration file.
; Farroad Godot port. Milestone 1 (the combat engine, FarroadCore.gd) runs
; headless via `godot --headless --script res://test/parity_test.gd`, the
; same command-line automation Godot ships for CI, mirroring how
; `node farroadsmoke.js` runs for the JS side of this project.
; Milestone 2 (UI/sprites) added a real main scene showing one hardcoded
; demo battle. Milestone 3 (the game loop) replaces it with Game.tscn --
; GameController.gd owns real game state and drives BattlePresenter wave
; after wave, so opening the project normally (no --headless) now plays an
; actual continuing, persistent game rather than one fixed fight.

config_version=5

[application]

config/name="Farroad"
config/features=PackedStringArray("4.7")
run/main_scene="res://scenes/Game.tscn"

[display]

; 360x800 is the DESIGN resolution, not a fixed output size -- meant to run
; on phones, which come in wildly different aspect ratios. stretch/mode
; canvas_items keeps 2D crisp while scaling; aspect=expand means a device
; whose aspect ratio differs from this gets MORE visible content on the
; wider/taller axis rather than letterboxing, so get_viewport_rect().size
; (what BattlePresenter.gd's layout is computed from, as fractions -- never
; a fixed pixel constant) reflects the real per-device canvas, not always
; exactly 360x800.
; 360x800 (~1:2.22, portrait) -- Ian's call: default to a phone held in
; PORTRAIT, not landscape. Swapped from the prior 800x360 landscape pair
; (same aspect ratio, just rotated) and window/handheld/orientation flipped
; to match, so the desktop window now opens tall-and-narrow like a phone
; actually held upright, rather than sideways.
window/size/viewport_width=360
window/size/viewport_height=800
window/stretch/mode="canvas_items"
window/stretch/aspect="expand"
window/handheld/orientation="portrait"
